    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Constitutional</td><td>Positive</td><td>Mild tiredness; low-grade temperature to 37.6 °C; eating and drinking normally</td></tr><tr><td>Ears, nose, mouth, and throat</td><td>Positive</td><td>Clear nasal discharge, congestion, and scratchy throat; no ear or facial pain</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Positive</td><td>Dry cough; no breathlessness, wheeze, or sputum</td></tr><tr><td>Genitourinary</td><td>Negative</td><td>No burning, frequency, new incontinence, or retention</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Positive</td><td>Night-time confusion on two nights after the antihistamine; no headache, weakness, or falls</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Negative</td><td>No hallucinations, agitation, or low mood</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>6 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
